# Real, measured problem this fixes: cosme-client/cosme-server's build (Dockerfile.endpoint,
# `context: .` relative to THIS file's directory) has no `COPY` instructions at all -- it only
# apt-get installs packages -- so it needs NOTHING from this directory at build time (media/ and
# endpoint-scripts/ are bind-mounted at RUNTIME instead, see docker-compose.yml). Without this
# file, every `docker compose build`/`up --build` still tars up the whole docker/ directory as
# build context regardless, including media/ (~9.8GB) and osrm-data/ (~14GB) once
# scripts/prepare_media_assets.sh and scripts/prepare_osrm.sh have populated them -- confirmed
# live this session: a routine rebuild (only docker-compose.yml + probe/Dockerfile had changed,
# NOT Dockerfile.endpoint) took ~53s just to send/unpack the context. The REPO-ROOT .dockerignore
# does NOT cover this -- it's scoped to docker/Dockerfile.backend's own build context (the repo
# root, `context: ..`), a different directory entirely, so it has no effect on this one.
media/
osrm-data/
# probe/ has its own separate build context (`context: ./probe`) -- not needed by
# Dockerfile.endpoint either.
probe/
.git/
